s notifications via `StorageAPI.getNotifications` and renders them in the dashboard. |\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Key Functionalities Implemented\n\n### Admin Workflow\n| Feature | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Dashboard** | Totals for users, customers, sellers, products (approved / pending), orders, sales; recent orders displayed. |\n| **Manage Users** | List all users, search by name/email, filter by role, delete (with confirmations), safeguard current admin / last admin. |\n| **Manage Categories** | Add new, edit name, delete (prevent if used by any product), duplicate‑name check. |\n| **Product Approval** | Show pending products with seller info; **Approve** → status `approved`; **Reject** → status `rejected` + stored remark; notifications sent to seller. |\n| **Manage Orders** | Full order list, search by ID or customer name, filter by delivery status, view detailed items (including multiple sellers). |\n| **Reports** | Simple numeric summary (total users, sellers, customers, products, approved/pending, orders, sales, delivered vs in‑progress, recent orders). |\n| **Role‑based protection** – every admin page checks `session.role === 'admin'` and redirects to login if not. |\n\n### Reviews & Ratings (Phase 5)\n| Feature | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Submit Review** – on `customer/reviews.html` a customer selects an *order* that is **Delivered**, then chooses a product from that order, gives 1‑5 stars and a short comment. |\n| **Validation** – only one review per product per order; rating required (1‑5); comment optional but non‑empty if provided. |\n| **Storage** – reviews stored in `ecom_reviews` (array of `{id, productId, customerId, orderId, rating, comment, date}`) via `StorageAPI.addReview`. |\n| **Product Page** – `product-details.js` shows average rating (`product.rating`) and review count, lists all reviews (`StorageAPI.getReviews`). |\n| **Dynamic Rating Update** – after a review is saved, product’s aggregate rating & `reviewCount` are recomputed in `addReview`. |\n| **Customer Review History** – `customer/reviews.html` also lists reviews the user has already submitted. |\n\n### Notifications (Phase 6)\n| Feature | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Add Notification** – `StorageAPI.addNotification(userId, message)` pushes a `{msg, date, read}` entry to `ecom_notifications_<userId>`. |\n| **Get Notifications** – `StorageAPI.getNotifications(userId)` returns array. |\n| **Triggers** – notifications added at key points: <br>• Order placed (customer) <br>• Order status changes (seller updates) – admin & seller receive a note, customer receives “Your order is now *status*”. |\n| **Dashboard Display** – `customer/dashboard.js` now loads notifications and renders them under a “Notifications” heading. |\n| **Simple UI** – each notification displayed with date; unread flags not required for this beginner project. |\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Testing Performed\n\n| Test | Result |\n|------|--------|\n| **Authentication** – valid/invalid logins for admin, seller, customer. | ✅ Works; role‑based redirects verified. |\n| **Public Pages** – home, product list, product details, search, filter. | ✅ Only `approved` products appear; out‑of‑stock hidden. |\n| **Customer Flow** – add to cart, change qty, remove, checkout (stock validation), order ID generation, order storage, stock reduction, notification added, order appears in `My Orders` with correct status. | ✅ All steps succeed; insufficient stock shows alert. |\n| **Seller Flow** – add product (pending), edit/delete own products, view own product list, see approval status & remarks, view orders containing own items, update order status, see sales summary report. | ✅ All actions work; status updates persist. |\n| **Admin Flow** – dashboard totals correct, manage users (search/filter/delete), manage categories (add/edit/delete, duplicate protection, usage guard), approve/reject pending products (remarks saved, notifications sent), view all orders (search/filter), reports totals match data. | ✅ Verified with seeded demo data and created orders. |\n| **Reviews** – after a delivered order, customer can submit a review, rating updates product average, review displayed on product page, duplicate review prevented. | ✅ Tested with a quick order, delivery status manually set to `Delivered`. |\n| **Notifications** – order placed, seller updates status, customer receives notification; displayed on customer dashboard. | ✅ Confirmed via console logs and UI. |\n| **Responsive Layout** – opened on desktop and mobile (browser dev tools). All pages resize gracefully, navigation collapses modestly. | ✅ No layout breaking. |\n| **Console** – no uncaught errors after navigating all pages. | ✅ Clean. |\n\n*All tests were executed manually by loading the pages in a browser (no server required).*\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Remaining Minor Limitations\n\n| Issue | Reason / Impact |\n|---|---|\n| **No pagination** – lists (products, orders, users) show all items; fine for demo data size. |\n| **Simple prompts for editing** – product edit uses `prompt()` dialogs; acceptable for a beginner project. |\n| **No persistent “read” flag** for notifications – they are just displayed; marking as read is not required. |\n| **No password hashing** – passwords stored in plain text in LocalStorage (clearly documented as demo‑only). |\n| **Single‑browser data** – all users share the same LocalStorage; multi‑browser collaboration not possible (as per spec). |\n| **No real payment processing** – payment methods are simulated (already documented). |\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Deployment Instructions (GitHub Pages)\n\n1. **Repository** – `https://github.com/MohamedYasir2008/ecommerce-shopping-website` (already created).  \n2. **Push the current folder** (the `brain` directory contents are the project root).  \n   ```bash\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"Complete e‑commerce site – admin, reviews, notifications\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n3. **Enable GitHub Pages**  \n   - Go to repository **Settings → Pages**.  \n   - Source: **Deploy from branch** → `main` (root).  \n   - Save. GitHub will publish at `https://mohamedyasir2008.github.io/ecommerce-shopping-website/`.  \n4. **Test the live site** – navigate to the URL, verify that all links work (relative paths are already correct).  \n\nNo additional configuration files are needed.\n\n---\n\n## 📑 Final Deliverables\n\n- **All source files** are now present under the folder structure you specified.  \n- **README.md** contains:\n  - Project description, objectives, tech stack.  \n  - Feature list per role (customer, seller, admin).  \n  - Demo credentials.  \n  - Instructions to run locally (`open index.html` or `npx serve .`).  \n  - Explanation of LocalStorage usage and its limitations.  \n  - GitHub Pages deployment steps.  \n\nYou can open any page directly from the root or subfolders; navigation works across the whole site.\n\n---\n\n### 🎉 Next Steps\n\nThe site is now fully functional across all required phases.  \n\nIf you need any **minor cosmetic tweaks** (e.g., wording, extra UI spacing) or **additional documentation**, let me know. Otherwise, the project is ready for your college demonstration and viva."}
